-- title:
--   Measurability of window values in the central idele parameter
-- statement:
--   The setting is a Galois extension $L/K$ of number fields whose Galois group is generated by a single automorphism $\sigma$ (the hypothesis `hgen` asserts that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$) and whose degree $[L:K]$ is prime (`hprime`). The group of ideles $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ carries a measurable structure which is the Borel structure of its topology, together with a Haar measure $\nu_{Z_K}$. Two finite sets $S_K, T$ of finite places of $K$ (height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$) are given, disjoint.
--
--   Throughout, for $u \in K^\times$ and $z \in (\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ the relevant group element is $\gamma(u,z) = z \cdot \mathrm{diag}(u,1) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, written in Lean as `centralScalar (𝓞 K) K z * diagUnits2 (Units.map (algebraMap K (AdeleRing (𝓞 K) K)) u) 1`; its archimedean image `AdelicLevel.glArch (𝓞 K) K γ(u,z)` and its component at a finite place $v$, `AdelicLevel.finComponent (𝓞 K) K v (AdelicLevel.glFin (𝓞 K) K γ(u,z))`, appear in all the local data below.
--
--   *Test functions and matching.* An archimedean factor $f_{a,K}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$ is assumed to be an arch test factor, i.e. to be given by a smooth function of the matrix entries read in the mixed space of $K$ and to have compact support; local factors $f_{S_K,v}$ for $v \in S_K$ are locally constant of compact support on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$. On the $L$-side, $\varphi_a$ is an arch test factor on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{L,\infty})$ and, for $v \in S_K$, $\varphi_{S,v}$ is locally constant of compact support on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$. The matching hypotheses `hmatchA` and `hmatchS` say that the pair $(\varphi_a \circ \mathrm{archIdentGL}, f_{a,K})$, respectively each pair $(\varphi_{S,v}, f_{S_K,v})$ for $v \in S_K$, satisfies the predicate `AreMatchingOn` for $\sigma$ over $\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty}$ with the Haar measures `archHaarL`, `archHaarK`, respectively over $K_v$ with `semiLocalHaar` and `localHaar`: whenever $\delta$ has regular semisimple norm string, $\gamma$ is regular semisimple, $y$ is a norm conjugator for $(\gamma,\delta)$, and Haar measures $\tau$ on the centraliser of $\gamma$ and $\tau'$ on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser of $\delta$ are coupled, then every twisted orbital integral of the $L$-side function at $\delta$ equals every orbital integral of the $K$-side function at $\gamma$; and if a regular semisimple $\gamma$ is not a norm, every orbital integral of the $K$-side function at $\gamma$ vanishes. Further local factors $f_{T,v}$ for $v \in T$ are locally constant of compact support (`hfT`), each admitting a matching semilocal partner (`hmatchT`), and at every place outside $S_K \cup T$ the indicator of `semiLocalIntegralSet K L v` matches the indicator of `localIntegralSet K v` (`hunit`).
--
--   *Global factorisation.* Functions $f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ and $f_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,\mathrm{fin}})$ are assumed (`hf`) to constitute a unit factorisation relative to $S_K \cup T$ with archimedean factor $f_{a,K}$ and local factors $v \mapsto f_{T,v}$ for $v \in T$ and $f_{S_K,v}$ otherwise: $f_{a,K}$ is an arch test factor, $f_f$ is locally constant with compact support, the local factors at places of $S_K \cup T$ are local test functions, $f_f(h)$ is the product of the local values over $S_K \cup T$ whenever all components of $h$ off $S_K \cup T$ lie in `localIntegralSet`, $f_f(h) = 0$ when some such component fails to, and $f(g) = f_{a,K}(g_\infty) f_f(g_{\mathrm{fin}})$.
--
--   *Splitting of the global integral.* A measure $\nu_A$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$ (for the Borel structure `glBorelOf`) and a real constant $c_G$ are given, with `hG` asserting: for every finite set $S$ of finite places and all functions $f', f_a, f_S$ such that $f_a$ is a.e. strongly measurable for $\nu_A$, each $f_S(v)$ for $v \in S$ is a.e. strongly measurable for `localHaar K v`, $f'(g)$ is the product of $f_a(g_\infty)$ with $\prod_{v \in S} f_S(v)(g_v)$ whenever all components of $g$ off $S$ lie in `localIntegralSet`, and $f'(g) = 0$ whenever some component off $S$ does not, one has $\int f' \, \mathrm{d}(\mathrm{adelicGLHaar})= c_G \bigl(\int f_a \,\mathrm{d}\nu_A\bigr) \prod_{v\in S} \int f_S(v) \,\mathrm{d}(\mathrm{localHaar}\,K\,v)$.
--
--   *Centraliser measures and their pinning.* A constant $c_{\tau K} > 0$ and measures $\tau_G(u,z)$ on the centraliser of $\gamma(u,z)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ are given; for $u \neq 1$ these are Haar (`hτG`) and, by `hτGc`, integration of any function over that centraliser equals $c_{\tau K}$ times its integral over pairs of ideles via $\mathrm{diag}$ against $\nu_{Z_K} \times \nu_{Z_K}$. Likewise $\tau_A(u,z)$ on the centraliser of the archimedean component and $\tau_F(u,z,v)$ on the local centraliser at $v$ are Haar for $u \neq 1$ (`hτA`, `hτF`), the latter normalised so that the preimage of `localIntegralSet K v` has mass $1$ (`hτF1`). A constant $c_T > 0$ and the hypothesis `hT` give the corresponding product formula for centraliser integrals: for $u \neq 1$ and data $W, W_a, W_S$ satisfying the analogous measurability, product and vanishing conditions relative to a finite set $S$, $\int W \,\mathrm{d}\tau_G(u,z) = c_T \bigl(\int W_a \,\mathrm{d}\tau_A(u,z)\bigr)\prod_{v \in S}\int W_S(v)\,\mathrm{d}\tau_F(u,z,v)$.
--
--   *The window values.* For $u \neq 1$: $I_A(u,z)$ is an orbital integral of $f_{a,K}$ at the archimedean component of $\gamma(u,z)$ for $\tau_A(u,z)$ and $\nu_A$ (`hIA`); $I_F(u,z,v)$, for $v \in S_K$, an orbital integral of $f_{S_K,v}$ at the $v$-component for $\tau_F(u,z,v)$ (`hIF`); $J_A(u,z)$ a weighted orbital integral of $f_{a,K}$ with weight $y \mapsto -\log \mathrm{archHeight}_K(y) - \log \mathrm{archHeight}_K(w_\infty y)$, $w$ the adelic Weyl element (`hJA`); $J_F(u,z,v)$, for $v \in S_K$, a weighted orbital integral of $f_{S_K,v}$ with the local weight (`hJF`). Further, $\nu_A'$ is a measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$, and the two measures are pinned by $\nu_A = \mathrm{archHaarK}\,K$ and $\nu_A' = \mathrm{archHaarL}\,K\,L$. Elements $\delta_A(u,z)$ and $\delta_F(u,z,v)$ are chosen so that, whenever the relevant component of $\gamma(u,z)$ is a norm, their $\sigma$-norm strings equal the image of that component under `toTensorGL` (`hδA`, `hδF`); $\tau_A'(u,z)$ and $\tau_F'(u,z,v)$ are Haar measures on the corresponding $\sigma$-twisted centralisers for $u \neq 1$ (`hτA'`, `hτF'`), with $\tau_A'$ coupled to $\tau_A$ through the conjugator $1$ on the norm locus (`hτA'c`) and $\tau_F'$ normalised to give mass $1$ to the preimage of `semiLocalIntegralSet K L v` (`hτF'1`). On the norm locus, $J_A'(u,z)$ is a twisted weighted orbital integral of $\varphi_a \circ \mathrm{archIdentGL}$ at $\delta_A(u,z)$ for $\nu_A'$ and $\tau_A'(u,z)$, with weight $y \mapsto -\log \mathrm{archHeight}_L(\mathrm{archIdentGL}\,y) - \log \mathrm{archHeight}_L(w_{L,\infty}\,\mathrm{archIdentGL}\,y)$ (`hJA'`), and $J_A'(u,z) = 0$ off that locus (`hJA'0`); similarly $J_F'(u,z,v)$, for $v \in S_K$, is a twisted weighted orbital integral of $\varphi_{S,v}$ at $\delta_F(u,z,v)$ for $\tau_F'(u,z,v)$ on the norm locus (`hJF'`) and vanishes off it (`hJF'0`). Finally $I_T(u,z,v)$, for $v \in T$, is an orbital integral of $f_{T,v}$ (`hIT`), and $I_U(u,z,v)$, for $v \notin S_K \cup T$, an orbital integral of the indicator function of `localIntegralSet K v` with value $1$ (`hIU`), both at the $v$-component of $\gamma(u,z)$ for $\tau_F(u,z,v)$.
--
--   The conclusion is that for every $u \in K^\times$ with $u \neq 1$ the following six assertions hold, measurability always being with respect to the Borel structure on $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$: the function $z \mapsto I_A(u,z)$ is measurable; the function $z \mapsto J_A(u,z)$ is measurable; the function $z \mapsto J_A'(u,z)$ is measurable; for every $v \in S_K$, the three functions $z \mapsto I_F(u,z,v)$, $z \mapsto J_F(u,z,v)$ and $z \mapsto J_F'(u,z,v)$ are measurable; for every $v \in T$, the function $z \mapsto I_T(u,z,v)$ is measurable; and for every finite place $v$ with $v \notin S_K$ and $v \notin T$, the function $z \mapsto I_U(u,z,v)$ is measurable.
--
--   This is a regularity step in the comparison of hyperbolic terms in the cyclic base-change trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$: it records that each of the archimedean, semilocal and finite-place orbital and weighted orbital values attached to the split family $z \cdot \mathrm{diag}(u,1)$ depends measurably on the central idele $z$, so that the family may be integrated over $z$. It is used in the assembly of the winding contribution, where the sum over central characters and the integral over $z$ are interchanged.
